{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-parabolic-hecke-subalgebra","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:parabolic-hecke-subalgebra","kind":"definition","title":"Parabolic Hecke subalgebra $H_\\lambda(q) \\hookrightarrow H_N(q)$","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-molecular-strand-partition","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-hecke-algebra-from-braiding"],"tags":["parabolic-subalgebra","young-subgroup","hecke-algebra","molecular","wedderburn"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Molecular.ParabolicHecke","text":"parabolic-hecke-subalgebra.md","leanSource":"parabolic-hecke-subalgebra.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:parabolic-hecke-subalgebra\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda = (n_1,\\dots,n_k)</code> be a strand-partition with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sum_i n_i = N</code>. The <strong>parabolic Hecke subalgebra</strong> is the tensor product</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  H_\\lambda(q) \\;=\\; H_{n_1}(q) \\otimes \\cdots \\otimes H_{n_k}(q) \\;\\hookrightarrow\\; H_N(q),</code></pre>\n<p>generated by the Hecke generators <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\sigma_j</code> that act within a single sub-unit block. The omitted generators, those joining two blocks, are the <strong>cross-block generators</strong>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/parabolic-hecke-subalgebra.md","heading":"Definition","number":"18.2.3","page":"b/def-parabolic-hecke-subalgebra","qa":{"counts":{"pass":82,"fail":0,"warn":1,"na":9,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.Molecular.ParabolicHecke","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/molecular-construction/parabolic-hecke-subalgebra.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
